  "slug": "zero-minor-binary-quartic-boundaries-are-automorphic-5e7e9377",
  "source": [],
  "statement": "Assume the Program 2 binary target-span-two reduction. If one of U=J(Q,R), V=J(P,R), or W=J(P,Q) vanishes, including the separate case R=0, then the quartic Keller map is a polynomial automorphism. Consequently the ordinary common-ramification filtration may be applied only after these zero-minor boundaries are removed.",
  "title": "Zero-Minor Binary Quartic Boundaries Are Automorphic",
  "visibility": "technical"
